================================================================
 AUTH AUDIT - COLUMN README / VALIDATION DICTIONARY
================================================================

PURPOSE
This report audits Microsoft Entra authentication method registration
and SMS-as-MFA likelihood. It is designed to work for both pre- and
post-combined (converged) registration, because the per-user data is
read from the unified authentication method store and the registration
report's computed signals.

----------------------------------------------------------------
COLUMN DICTIONARY
----------------------------------------------------------------

UserPrincipalName
  Source : Get-MgUser
  Meaning: User principal name.
  Notes  : Directory value.

Email
  Source : Get-MgUser (Mail)
  Meaning: Primary email address.
  Notes  : May be empty.

AccountEnabled
  Source : Get-MgUser
  Meaning: Whether the account is enabled.
  Notes  : Used by the "Enabled" scope filter.

Domain
  Source : Derived from UPN
  Meaning: UPN domain suffix.
  Notes  : Parsed after the @ character.

PerUserMfaState
  Source : beta /users/{id}/authentication/requirements (perUserMfaState)
  Meaning: Legacy per-user MFA state.
  Notes  : enabled / enforced / disabled, or Unavailable.

IsMfaRegistered
  Source : Authentication methods registration report (isMfaRegistered)
  Meaning: User has registered at least one MFA method.
  Notes  : From the unified registration report.

IsMfaCapable
  Source : Authentication methods registration report (isMfaCapable)
  Meaning: User is MFA-capable per the EFFECTIVE policy.
  Notes  : Reflects both legacy and modern policy. Covers BOTH pre- and
           post-combined registration.

TenantSmsPolicyState
  Source : beta authenticationMethodConfigurations/Sms (state)
  Meaning: Tenant-level SMS authentication method policy state.
  Notes  : Queried ONCE per run. If SMS is scoped to specific groups
           rather than all users, this tenant value can OVERSTATE
           per-user availability.

MobilePhoneRegistered
  Source : Get-MgUserAuthenticationPhoneMethod (mobile) OR
           registration report methodsRegistered (mobilePhone / sms)
  Meaning: A mobile phone method is registered for the user.
  Notes  : Office numbers are voice-only and are EXCLUDED. Generic
           "phone" matching is intentionally not used.

SmsMfaLikelyAvailable
  Source : Derived (composite)
  Meaning: LIKELIHOOD that SMS can serve as an MFA method for the user.
  Logic  : IsMfaCapable = True
           AND MobilePhoneRegistered = True
           AND TenantSmsPolicyState = enabled
  Notes  : This is a LIKELIHOOD / CAPABILITY signal, NOT proof that SMS
           was used, and NOT an SMS-specific guarantee. A registered
           mobile number can serve SMS or voice depending on policy.
           Definitive confirmation that SMS was usable/used as MFA
           requires Microsoft Entra sign-in log validation
           (authenticationMethodsUsed / authentication details).
           Also subject to the group-scoping caveat under
           TenantSmsPolicyState.

SecurityQuestionsRegistered
  Source : securityQuestionAuthenticationMethod object OR
           registration report methodsRegistered
  Meaning: Whether security questions are registered.
  Notes  : NOT inferred from IsSsprRegistered.

AllRegisteredAuthMethods
  Source : Get-MgUserAuthenticationMethod + normalized phone methods
  Meaning: Normalized list of registered authentication methods.
  Notes  : Sorted unique; semicolon-joined.

PhoneType
  Source : Get-MgUserAuthenticationPhoneMethod
  Meaning: Phone type for this row.
  Notes  : mobile / alternateMobile / office, or None.

PhoneNumber
  Source : Get-MgUserAuthenticationPhoneMethod
  Meaning: Registered phone number.
  Notes  : One row per phone method.

----------------------------------------------------------------
KEY CAVEATS
----------------------------------------------------------------
1. SmsMfaLikelyAvailable is a LIKELIHOOD signal, not proof. To confirm
   SMS was actually used as MFA, cross-reference Microsoft Entra
   sign-in logs (authenticationMethodsUsed / authentication details).

2. TenantSmsPolicyState reflects tenant-level state. If SMS is enabled
   only for specific groups, this value can overstate per-user
   availability. Resolve includeTargets vs. group membership for exact
   per-user precision.

3. Office phone numbers are voice-only and are excluded from
   MobilePhoneRegistered and from SmsMfaLikelyAvailable.

4. IsMfaCapable covers both pre- and post-combined registration because
   it reflects the effective policy and the unified method store.
================================================================
